       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make 6,400 mg/day safe.\n\nThe order may be a typo or a mix-up with the daily total. Common options are:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that, and I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
