       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the clinical rationale from here. 6,400 mg/day is twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum and has no established indication in adults. The risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm is high enough that I don't want to put it in the system on my own.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** I can enter 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) right now, or any lower regimen.\n- **Get a second review.** Discuss the regimen with pharmacy or the relevant specialist, such as ID, rheumatology, or pulmonary. If they support it, they can document the rationale and an override.\n- **Enter it yourself.** If you decide to proceed, you can enter it directly with the required override and documentation. That way it goes through the hospital's high-dose verification process.\n\nIf there's a specific protocol behind this dose, tell me which one. It may be a different dose or frequency than what I have, and I can enter it if it fits. I can also add a note to the order, such as monitoring parameters."
